# Did the human actually ask to remove THIS content?

The script already settled the clear cases: pure additions passed, and a
removal with no deletion/rewrite intent anywhere this turn was refused
outright. You are reached only for the residue — content WAS removed, and a
human message this turn DID voice something like a deletion or a rewrite, but
often loosely ("clean this up", "rewrite it properly"). Your single job: does
that ask authorize dropping THESE specific lines?

